<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kirkuk</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kirkuk is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tigris">Tigris</a>, on the site of ancient Arrapha, capital of a Hurrian kingdom in the 15th and 14th centuries BCE. Its citadel mound has been occupied for millennia. The discovery of oil at nearby <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baba-gurgur">Baba Gurgur</a> in 1927 made it the centre of Iraq's northern oil industry, and its mixed Kurdish, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkmen">Turkmen</a> and Arab population has made its status disputed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kirkuk.jpg" alt="Kirkuk" width="320" height="238" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chad.r.hill at English Wikipedia · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kirkuk_citadel.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
